Procedural next moves
=====================
1. Build one common 'lift feasibility' data model:
   boundary totals, candidate hidden cells, local gates, surviving allocations, and proof owner.
2. Polynomial side: extend HYP-2452 with bounded ILP/SAT degree-6 lifts.
3. LRC side: turn Q27/Pisano one-stranger rows into multi-stranger allocation ledgers.
4. Unit-distance side: classify product-reducible versus Moser-irreducible extension fibers at N=27/28.
5. Code side: encode [72,36,16] minimum-word supports as binary incidence lifts over the 78/90 address.

Assumption challenge
====================
Alternate vertices considered: polynomial rows, factor coefficients, prime tokens,
LRC runners, residues, Q27 divisors, unit-distance points, unit directions,
Moser ears, triangular endpoints, code supports, Fourier modes, and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices are carriers/proof obligations because they preserve the predicate
'does a hidden lift exist?' across all four domains.  The quotient destroys
domain-specific geometry, so each transfer must reattach its local side channels
before being treated as evidence.
